{"filePath": "/Users/m0c0qiy/Downloads/IISC/IISC Managerial Economics/term-paper/assignment-2/main.tex", "newString": "\mine{How did exits, acquisitions and mergers between 2015 and 2026 change concentration in India's scheduled domestic aviation market when airlines with the same owner are counted as one firm, and has the market moved from an oligopoly of several airlines to a lasting asymmetric duopoly, based on set thresholds?}

\textbf{O1.} To measure monthly concentration using brand-level, ownership-level and modified \HHI{} along with \CRtwo{}, and to estimate how much each exit and merger changed it. Since we have no fare data, we limit our claims to market structure.\\
\mine{\textbf{O2.} To find out which airlines took over the passengers and seats left by Jet Airways (2019) and Go First (2023), whether access to slots and aircraft explains this, and how the Tata Group's consolidation compares with CCI's own merger review.}\\
\textbf{O3.} To check whether airlines that entered after 2015 managed to grow and stay in the market, by looking at their market share over time, how long they lasted and how they ended up (still flying, shut down or merged).\\
\textbf{O4.} To test whether the market meets set duopoly thresholds for \CRtwo{}, \HHI{}, share gap and fringe share, to see whether national figures hide single-airline routes among the top 20--30 routes (if city-pair data is available), and to measure rivals' spare capacity in December 2025 and the capacity share where IndiGo is the only or main operator.", "oldString": "\mine{How did major consolidation events (exits, acquisitions and mergers) reshape concentration in India's scheduled domestic passenger aviation market between 2015 and 2026 once common ownership is taken into account, and has the oligopoly narrowed into a durable asymmetric duopoly, judged against pre-defined thresholds?}

\textbf{O1.} To track monthly market structure with three concentration series (brand \HHI{}, ownership \HHI{} and modified \HHI{}), \CRtwo{} and the effective number of firms, to estimate the step change at each exit and merger, and to show how much brand-level counting understates concentration, limiting claims to market structure as no fare data is available.\\
\mine{\textbf{O2.} To measure which airline groups absorbed the passengers and seat capacity of Jet Airways (2019) and Go First (2023) after they exited, to explain these shifts with slot and fleet evidence, and to assess the Tata Group consolidation (2022--2024) against CCI's combination order.}\\
\textbf{O3.} To examine whether airlines entering the market after 2015 grew into meaningful and persistent competitors, using their market-share growth, survival and eventual outcome (still operating, exited or merged).\\
