where $\text{Index}_t$ is, in turn, Brand-\HHI{}, Ownership-\HHI{} and \MHHI{}; $\text{Post}_{kt}$ marks the four events (Jet Airways exit, Tata acquisition, Go First exit, late-2024 mergers); $\gamma_k$ is the step at event $k$; and standard errors use the Newey--West correction (12 lags) for autocorrelated monthly data \parencite{neweywest1987}. Comparing $\gamma_k$ across the three series shows how far each event's measured effect depends on how firms are counted.

