\textbf{\objref{2}.} Both exiting airlines declined before they stopped flying, so the before-windows already include part of the shift and the absorption figures may understate it. Other changes overlap the windows: Akasa Air's ramp-up and SpiceJet's decline during the Go First window, and the end of COVID-19 during the January 2022 comparison. The Jet Airways after-window is ten months to avoid the pandemic. The Cournot markups are illustrative, as we have no fare or cost data. CCI's market is the city pair and ours is national, so the two measure different things, and the share triggers in the CCI commitments are redacted.

