\textbf{\objref{2}.}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=2em]
    \item \textbf{H3: Partially supported.} IndiGo absorbed the largest share of passengers after both exits, and a larger share after Go First (66.0\%) than after Jet Airways (37.7\%); but after Jet Airways, SpiceJet took more of the seat-km because it received the vacated slots.
    \item \textbf{H4: Supported.} IndiGo's gain accounts for more than half of the rise in \HHI{} after both exits, on both measures.
\end{itemize}
Both results match \textcite{grosche2020concentration}, who find that concentration in German air transport rose after Air Berlin's bankruptcy and that the largest group, Lufthansa, became more dominant, as IndiGo did here.

