\subsection{Research question and objectives}
How did major consolidation events (exits, acquisitions and mergers) reshape concentration in India's scheduled domestic passenger aviation market between 2015 and 2026 once common ownership is taken into account, and has the oligopoly narrowed into a durable asymmetric duopoly, judged against pre-defined thresholds?

\begin{description}[leftmargin=2.2em,style=sameline,font=\normalfont\bfseries]
    \item[\hypertarget{objective:1}{O1.}] Lasting effect of the four consolidation events on brand, ownership and modified \HHI{}, \CRtwo{} and the effective number of firms; size of the grouping and partial-ownership effects.
    \item[\hypertarget{objective:2}{O2.}] Which groups absorbed Jet Airways' and Go First's passengers and capacity, and how much the Tata consolidation raised concentration through common ownership alone, read against CCI's combination order.
    \item[\hypertarget{objective:3}{O3.}] Whether the nine entrants since 2015 became meaningful and persistent competitors.
    \item[\hypertarget{objective:4}{O4.}] Whether IndiGo and the Air India Group form an asymmetric duopoly nationally and on the top 20 routes, and how resilient the market is to IndiGo disruption.
\end{description}

